WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.790
 We're all persuading
all the time.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.460
Sales and persuasion
is part of our lives.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.710
It's like the weather.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.425
No matter what you
do, you are in sales.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.100
I've spent the last 20 years
researching and writing

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.500
about two obsessions
in my life--

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.720
persuasion and motivation.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.080
Persuasion is not some
kind of magical thing

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.100
that we do to manipulate people.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.040
It's not about tricking people.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.470
It's actually more
beautiful than that.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.540
Whether you are an entrepreneur
trying to raise money,

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.540
whether you're an employee
trying to convince your boss,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.008
whether you're a parent
trying to persuade your kid,

00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:45.550
I'm going to show
you how to do that.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.870
This approach is
built on science.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.470
I want to show you
how our brains work.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.870
There's a lot of
research on mimicry.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.870
Waiters and waitresses who
repeated the order back word

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:59.980
for word earned 70% more tips.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.830
Mimic people's language and
you'll see a difference.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.590
I think a lot of people approach
pitching in the wrong way.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:09.040
Two scholars went to a whole
set of Hollywood pitch meetings

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.050
to see what was effective
and what was not.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:14.080
If you look at the research,
it is overwhelming.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.200
The pitches that were
effective invite the other side

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.750
in as a collaborator,
period, full stop.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:27.310
A cognitive bias is a
glitch in the human mind.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.290
We all are subject to it.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.460
We have to watch for it.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:35.110
Because in 99 times out of 100,
it's going to lead us astray.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:38.170
If you think about sales
and persuasion and influence

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:41.560
in a fresh way, you can be
extraordinarily effective

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.150
and do something
really important

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:47.900
for the world, other people,
and ultimately yourself.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.800
I'm Daniel Pink and
this is my MasterClass.

